1.5 Modified Variational Formulations
We shall present in this section modified variational principles associated to saddlepoint problems or more general mixed methods. We shall distinguish between augmented formulations and perturbed formulations. In the following, augmented formulations will correspond to a modification of the variational formulation of the continuous problem. This will be done so that the solution is not changed (under perhaps some regularity conditions). The discretised versions will however in general be different. On the other hand, perturbed formulations will be meaningful only on a discrete problem. The rationale behind the introduction of these modified formulations is that they will have, for some discretisations, a better behaviour than the original one, in particular with respect to stability issues.


